"""Short notes for genes that can appear in the top 10. Every PMID here was checked against PubMed.

Each entry: (what the gene does, does it make sense as a marker). The report builder refuses to run if a
top 10 gene has no entry, so no gene reaches the write-up without a checked note.
"""

NOTES = {
    "KRT5": ("Keratin 5 is a structural protein of the basal cells of the skin; when it is faulty, these cells break and the skin blisters (PMID 20030639).",
             "Yes, for LUSC. CK5/6 is one of a four stain panel used to subtype lung cancer biopsies (PMID 25120805), and KRT5 with AGR2 separates LUSC from LUAD by staining (PMID 34150027)."),
    "KRT6A": ("Keratin 6A is a keratin that the skin switches on after wounding (PMID 10866680).",
              "Yes, for LUSC. It was named as a possible marker that separates LUSC from LUAD in public expression data (PMID 29069744)."),
    "KRT6B": ("Keratin 6B is the second form of keratin 6; it can also be switched on in wounded skin (PMID 10866680).",
              "Yes, for LUSC. It was named with KRT6A as a possible marker that separates LUSC from LUAD (PMID 29069744)."),
    "DSG3": ("Desmoglein 3 is a desmosome protein that glues squamous cells together; it is the target of the autoantibodies in pemphigus (PMID 28492232).",
             "Yes, for LUSC. It is a sensitive and specific stain for lung squamous carcinoma (PMID 19342368) and was confirmed by staining tumours (PMID 26380766)."),
    "DSC3": ("Desmocollin 3 is a protein of the desmosome junctions that hold the cells of layered epithelia together (PMID 19287461).",
             "Yes, for LUSC. It marks squamous differentiation (PMID 19287461), and a meta analysis lists it among stains for lung squamous carcinoma (PMID 35126682)."),
    "TP63": ("p63 is the master transcription factor of basal and squamous cells; its short form (p40) is what pathologists stain (PMID 22056955).",
             "Yes, for LUSC. p40 staining is 100% sensitive and 98% specific for lung squamous carcinoma (PMID 22056955); TP63 is often amplified in LUSC (PMID 22960745)."),
    "SOX2": ("SOX2 is a lineage transcription factor that is amplified and needed for growth in squamous cancers (PMID 19801978).",
             "Yes, for LUSC (PMID 19801978, 32905832)."),
    "CLCA2": ("CLCA2 is a protein involved in moving chloride across cell membranes (PMID 25548429).",
              "Yes, for LUSC. As a stain it was found in 65% of squamous carcinomas and 1% of adenocarcinomas (PMID 25548429)."),
    "CALML3": ("CALML3 is a calmodulin like calcium sensor made by differentiating skin cells (PMID 23638045, 18818677).",
               "Yes, for LUSC. It was confirmed by staining as a LUSC marker (PMID 26380766)."),
    "S100A7": ("S100A7 (psoriasin) is a calcium binding protein made by skin cells that also draws in immune cells (PMID 9693957).",
               "Yes, for LUSC. It was reported as a biomarker of lung squamous carcinoma (PMID 25745359)."),
    "PKP1": ("Plakophilin 1 is a desmosome plaque protein of squamous cells (PMID 31809668).",
             "Yes, for LUSC. It helps separate squamous from adenocarcinoma (PMID 31809668) and drives MYC in LUSC (PMID 35182388)."),
    "SERPINB13": ("SERPINB13 is a protease inhibitor made in squamous epithelium (PMID 19569240).",
                  "Likely, for LUSC. It fits the squamous programme; it was studied in head and neck squamous cancer (PMID 19569240), not as a lung stain."),
    "NECTIN1": ("Nectin 1 is a cell adhesion protein of skin cells and a direct target of p63 (PMID 25387952, 27516130).",
                "Likely, for LUSC. Its link to p63 fits the squamous programme; I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
    "CSTA": ("Cystatin A is a protease inhibitor of the skin; losing it makes skin peel (PMID 21944047).",
             "Likely, for LUSC. It fits the skin like programme of LUSC; I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
    "HNF1B": ("HNF1B is a transcription factor; faults in it are the most common single gene cause of kidney malformation (PMID 25536396).",
              "Yes, for LUAD, with a caveat. Normal lung and LUAD keep it, while LUSC silences it by DNA methylation (PMID 29169318, 32117905); because normal lung also has it, a stain would have to be read in tumour cells only."),
    "NAPSA": ("Napsin A is a protease that processes surfactant protein B in type II alveolar cells (PMID 13129928).",
              "Yes, for LUAD. It is a standard stain and is more sensitive than TTF-1 (87% vs 64%) for lung adenocarcinoma (PMID 22288963)."),
    "NKX2-1": ("NKX2-1 (TTF-1) is the lineage transcription factor of the lung's terminal respiratory unit (PMID 12023581, 17616654).",
               "Yes, for LUAD. TTF-1 is a standard stain, kept in about 72% of adenocarcinomas (PMID 12023581)."),
    "SFTA2": ("SFTA2 is a small secreted peptide made mainly in the lung (PMID 22768197).",
              "Yes, for LUAD. It was reported among genes that separate LUAD from LUSC (PMID 29069744)."),
    "MLPH": ("Melanophilin links the transport motor myosin Va to Rab27a to move vesicles inside cells (PMID 16473608).",
             "Yes, for LUAD. It was confirmed by staining as a LUAD marker (PMID 26380766)."),
    "SPDEF": ("SPDEF is a transcription factor that turns airway cells into mucus making goblet cells (PMID 25866971).",
              "Yes, for LUAD. Mucus making is a glandular trait; SPDEF controls the mucin MUC5AC in lung cancer cells (PMID 34139546)."),
    "AGR2": ("AGR2 is a gene that FOXM1 switches on as lung tumours turn into mucus making (mucinous) adenocarcinoma (PMID 29267283).",
             "Yes, for LUAD. With KRT5 it separates LUAD from LUSC by staining (PMID 34150027)."),
    "MACC1": ("MACC1 is a regulator of the MET growth signal that promotes spread of cancer (PMID 19787327).",
              "Likely, for LUAD. It is high in lung adenocarcinoma and linked to recurrence after surgery (PMID 21093878); it is not used as a stain."),
    "BCL2L15": ("BCL2L15 (Bfk) is a weak cell death protein of the BCL2 family (PMID 12700646).",
                "Unclear. A PubMed search found no study of BCL2L15 in lung cancer subtyping; its strong, replicated LUAD pattern makes it a new lead, not an established marker."),
    "SLC44A4": ("SLC44A4 carries thiamine pyrophosphate (a vitamin B1 form) into gut lining cells (PMID 31639155).",
                "Unclear. It fits a glandular cell type, but I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
    "SUCLG2": ("SUCLG2 is part of the mitochondrial enzyme succinyl CoA ligase in the Krebs cycle (PMID 18392745).",
               "Unclear as a stain. It was studied as a driver of mitochondrial changes in LUAD (PMID 37904651)."),
    "GPR39": ("GPR39 is a zinc sensing receptor on the cell surface (PMID 33918078).",
              "Unclear. I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
    "PRMT1": ("PRMT1 adds methyl groups to arginines on many proteins (PMID 37922507).",
              "Unclear. It is a broad regulator, studied for prognosis in lung cancer (PMID 38125466), not as a subtype stain."),
    "MUC3A": ("MUC3A is a membrane mucin of the intestine (PMID 11289722).",
              "Likely, for LUAD, as a glandular mucin; it was studied in LUAD progression (PMID 33249400), not as a stain."),
    "ELFN2": ("ELFN2 is a cell surface protein that pairs with glutamate receptors at nerve synapses (PMID 33790745).",
              "Unclear. Its LUAD pattern is strong here and holds in CPTAC-3, but I found no lung subtyping study."),
    "SIAH2": ("SIAH2 is an E3 ubiquitin ligase that tunes the low oxygen response (PMID 19372575).",
              "Unclear. I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
    "BNC1": ("Basonuclin 1 is a transcription factor of basal epithelial cells and a direct target of p63, the main squamous cell factor (PMID 21741828).",
             "Likely, for LUSC. It was among the top genes that separate lung squamous carcinoma from adenocarcinoma in another expression study (PMID 32360590), but I found no study that tests it as a lung stain."),
}
